# Remote denylist feeds for aur-cooldown. Off by default; to enable, copy this
# file to ~/.config/aur-cooldown/denylist-feeds and uncomment/add URLs.
#
# Each URL must return plain text: one AUR package name per line, '#' comments
# allowed. Tracked packages appearing on any feed are frozen (never upgraded)
# until they drop off the feed. Feeds are fetched by `observe` and `refresh`;
# on fetch failure the previous cache is kept.
#
# Consuming a third-party list is safe here because a denylist can only
# withhold installs, never cause one. A wrong or stale feed makes you wait,
# nothing more.
#
# Community-maintained campaign list (aur-general mailing list + official
# incident notes, consolidated):
#
#https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lenucksi/aur-malware-check/main/data/campaigns/aur-infected/packages.txt
#
# During an active incident, the official Arch pad for that campaign (announced
# on archlinux.org/news and aur-general) can be added directly.
